ZERO.BILLION-TESTS / verification campaign

PURPOSE
  Drive the ZERO core through a reproducible multi-billion-case campaign.

TARGET
  2^32 = 4,294,967,296 logical test cases.

EXECUTION MODEL
  256 independent shards.
  Each shard owns exactly 2^24 = 16,777,216 case identifiers.
  case_id = shard << 24 | local_id.

NO RANDOMNESS DEPENDENCY
  Inputs are generated from case_id by a specified deterministic bijective mixer.
  Every failing case is therefore reproducible from one integer.

CAMPAIGN LAYERS
  L0 parser / representation invariants
  L1 transition invariants
  L2 mutation and rollback
  L3 unknown preservation
  L4 history integrity
  L5 capability isolation
  L6 information-flow isolation
  L7 resource exhaustion
  L8 adversarial transformations
  L9 replay equivalence
  L10 metamorphic relations
  L11 compiler/implementation differential checks
  L12 boundary and hostile-device simulations

PROMOTION GATE
  A single failure blocks PROVEN.
  A timeout is not a PASS.
  A crash is not a PASS.
  An unexecuted shard is not a PASS.
  Missing artifact is not a PASS.

EVIDENCE
  Each shard emits:
    shard id
    first case
    last case
    executed count
    failure count
    failing case ids
    implementation hash
    specification hash
    toolchain hash
    timestamp

GLOBAL RESULT
  The campaign is EXHAUSTIVELY-TESTED only when all 256 shards have
  independently verified PASS artifacts for the same source/specification digest.

IMPORTANT
  This campaign is stress/exhaustive testing of finite generated domains.
  It is not by itself a mathematical proof of arbitrary ZERO programs.
